ged it's it's  not enough there will need to be more  but you correct  senate majority leader mitch mcconnell  president trump neither have endorsed  this  have you spoken to either of them are  you expecting them to come on board  well i think they both give encouraging  signs that something needs to be done  and they're looking and they're very  encouraging i heard that leader mitch  mcconnell  has said that basically bipartisan a  deal  can be done and that's very encouraging  because we are prepared to do a deal  you'll see what we call section by  section be  rolled out this afternoon probably in  the three four o'clock range  the people been drafting the staff's  been working around the clock  and we just have a couple more things  we're waiting on more information but  we'll get 90 percent of it out today  so the american public can see how we  want to roll this out well senator  manchin i know you said you're  optimistic and a lot of people are  counting on this  but and christmas break is coming up if  it's not done should christmas break be  delayed when you have so many people who  are in pain are just waiting and hoping  on you guys to  get this done i don't know how i don't  know how any senator could go home or  any congress person could return home  not making every effort how can you look  at people that will be displaced  be evicted or in hunger lines people  that you've never seen in long lines for  food assistance  all the things that were hurting  businesses that closed down that might  not ever open back  up i don't know how you can go home and  say well i'm sorry we had to come home  for christmas vacation  well they're going to say take a  vacation don't even go back that's what  i would say  will direct cash payments be included in  this because there's  a bipartisan push both like from josh  holding on the right bernie sanders on  the left no  sure anything i understand that remember  i used the word emergency  yeah yeah we had a hard time having our  republicans move  off the 500 billion and then we've had a  hard time for democrats to come down  below  1.2 yeah everyone has moved in an area  says can we just  least meet the emergency needs of  america and if you look at everything  that is going to be eliminated as of  december 31st  that's where your priorities must be for  an emergency relief package  that's what we've done and i and joe  biden said this is a down payment  uh we're president joe biden coming in  we're he'll come back and  lay out a new plan of what he thinks it  takes to have this economy recover and  stay on a course  vaccines are coming out people's spirits  will be lifted  we just got to get through a very  difficult first quarter the most  challenging we've ever faced  well you know the congress has only  passed one stimulus bill so far and  everybody agrees people are hurting  why is this so difficult why haven't why  hasn't congress done more at this point  without finger pointing it must be very  frustrating to you too  oh my it's so frustrating but i think  what's happened gail  is people are looking at all the stock  markets are soaring unemployment has  come down  some what they're not talking about is  still the unemployed and underemployed  people that went back to work that can't  make their full paycheck because the  economy is not there if they worked in  the restaurant entertainment or any of  these venues  so this is a tremendous problem that we  have people being evicted  we know the landlord's trying to play  their mortgage payment when a person is  evicted there's no money  we're trying to address every uh thing  that we need to be addressed today that  we think that could have been done  better the first time  we're learning from that and trying to  correct those mistakes i can tell you  this i am so proud of the democrats and  republicans  we're all friends we've always been  friends we just don't always sit down  and work together  for the last three weeks we've been  hooked to the hip probably four to five  six hours a day  back and forth on zooms and and it's  encouraging it really is and a bicameral  too  from our house members have been so  constructive all right senator joe  manchin thank you very much for being  with us this morning we hope this deal  gets done  yes let's remember that word friends yes  let's remember that f word friends  that's right kale i can't wait to see  you all in person again yeah  for sure thank you

